# PERMS.SCR - which commands run in which session state and at which
# user level: 400 before LOGIN, 404 while a password change is pending,
# 203 below the command's level or on a read-only station, 402 for a
# command that needs the system to itself while other sessions are
# open.  An unknown command is 101 in every state; so is a group word
# alone or with an unknown second word.  A command that passes the gate gets its own
# answer (data, +OK, or an error of the command such as 200), never one
# of the gate's codes.

# Not yet HELLO: every command but HELLO PING VER BYE is 400, LOGIN too.
> FOO
< -ERR 101 unknown command
> ITEM
< -ERR 101 unknown command
> ITEM FOO 1
< -ERR 101 unknown command
> ASSY
< -ERR 101 unknown command
> MAINT FOO 1
< -ERR 101 unknown command
> LOGIN ADMIN admin
< -ERR 400 HELLO or LOGIN required
> ITEM GET 1
< -ERR 400 HELLO or LOGIN required
> MAINT LIST 1
< -ERR 400 HELLO or LOGIN required
> ADMIN PACK
< -ERR 400 HELLO or LOGIN required

# HELLO but no LOGIN.
> HELLO PC1
< +OK
> FOO
< -ERR 101 unknown command
> USER BAR
